    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="0898" n="1732" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.711/18</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-09T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 9, 11 a.m. Department compliments you upon successfully arranging for
                    censorship in Cuba of all mail in transit by Spanish steamers between Mexico and
                    Spain and vice versa. It is important that this censorship be very carefully
                    performed under direct American control and supervision.</p>
                <p>Report fully by pouch upon present censorship conditions—how arranged and how
                    functioning and position and work of American officers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
